<main>


<section class="section why why--wide" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="band" data-band="forumInfo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="section__inner">
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="why__intro t-h5" data-reveal>
        <h2 id="why-title" class="visually-hidden">Why attend</h2>
        <p>In the age of transformative AI, we need shared infrastructure for human welfare and agency. <span class="ink-60">AI is making a new generation of fortunes, and nobody has settled what they should fund or who gets to decide.</span></p>
        <p><span class="ink-60">Right now those decisions are being made by a very small circle.</span><span class="ink-40"> Economists and engineers rarely share a conversation, and neither do constitutional lawyers and the teams training the models, or funders and the people who will live with the results. There is still time to widen the circle and put sovereignty, governance, and agency on one table, with the people building the systems and the people funding them.</span></p>
        <p class="ink-20">This March we'll spend two days doing that in focused sessions and open debate, some of it off the record, to start lasting collaborations and research.</p>
      </div>

      <nav class="iam" aria-label="Go to your section">
        <p class="iam__label">I am a…</p>
        <div class="iam__pills">
          <a class="iam__pill" href="#card-funders" data-choose="card-funders">funder</a>
          <a class="iam__pill" href="#card-researchers" data-choose="card-researchers">researcher</a>
          <a class="iam__pill" href="#card-policy" data-choose="card-policy">policymaker</a>
          <a class="iam__pill" href="#card-founders" data-choose="card-founders">founder</a>
        </div>
      </nav>

      <div class="why__cards">

        
        <article class="feature" id="card-funders">
          <div class="feature__body">
            <p class="feature__label t-meta">( Funders )</p>
            <h3 class="feature__headline t-h4-light">Back what the AI age needs, and learn how to tell whether it worked.</h3>
            <ul class="feature__lines">
              <li>Talk to founders and researchers before their work turns into a proposal.</li>
              <li>Compare notes with funders in your field and find partners to co-fund with.</li>
              <li>Take part in live funding rounds where the room decides the allocation.</li>
              <li>Join the private dinner on the eve of the Forum, included with the Patron pass.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="feature__footer">
              <div class="feature__actions">
                <a class="btn btn--dark t-label" data-url="forumPass" href="#">
                  Get the institutional pass
                  <svg class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg>
                </a>
                <a class="btn btn--outline t-label" data-url="partnerOnEvent" href="#">
                  Partner with us
                  <svg class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg>
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="feature__media">
            <img src="../../assets/img/forum/why-funders.jpg" alt="Funders in conversation over dinner at a Funding the Commons gathering" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </article>

        
        <article class="feature feature--flip" id="card-researchers">
          <div class="feature__body">
            <p class="feature__label t-meta">( Researchers and governance designers )</p>
            <h3 class="feature__headline t-h4-light">Put your model, policy, or governance design in front of the people who will use it and the people who can break it.</h3>
            <ul class="feature__lines">
              <li>Test your mechanism in workshops with the funders who would pay for it and the founders who would run it.</li>
              <li>Argue your case on and off the record with policymakers and engineers.</li>
              <li>Give a recorded main-stage talk once your work is ready for a wider audience.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="feature__footer">
              <a class="btn btn--outline btn--full t-label" data-url="applyToSpeak" href="#">
                Apply to speak
                <svg class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="feature__media">
            <img src="../../assets/img/forum/why-researchers.jpg" alt="A builder at work across three screens during a Funding the Commons residency" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </article>

        
        <article class="feature" id="card-policy">
          <div class="feature__body">
            <p class="feature__label t-meta">( Policy and public infrastructure )</p>
            <h3 class="feature__headline t-h4-light">Shape the rules for AI systems while they can still change, with the teams building them.</h3>
            <ul class="feature__lines">
              <li>Debate who should own the data, compute, and models that schools, clinics, and city services will run on.</li>
              <li>Meet peers from city governments, agencies, and international organizations already running public AI projects.</li>
              <li>Sit down with the funders deciding which digital public infrastructure to back next.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="feature__footer">
              <a class="btn btn--outline btn--full t-label" data-url="tickets" href="#">
                Get your tickets
                <svg class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="feature__media">
            <img src="../../assets/img/forum/why-policy.jpg" alt="A fireside chat on stage at Funding the Commons San Francisco" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </article>

        
        <article class="feature feature--flip" id="card-founders">
          <div class="feature__body">
            <p class="feature__label t-meta">( Founders )</p>
            <h3 class="feature__headline t-h4-light">Find funders, users, and partners for work a market alone won't pay for.</h3>
            <ul class="feature__lines">
              <li>Learn how other founders keep open infrastructure funded.</li>
              <li>Hand your prototype to the people it's for and hear what's missing.</li>
              <li>Stay part of a community that keeps working between gatherings, through residencies and fellowships.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="feature__footer">
              <div class="feature__actions">
                <a class="btn btn--dark t-label" data-url="applyToSpeak" href="#">
                  Apply to speak
                  <svg class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg>
                </a>
                <a class="btn btn--outline t-label" data-url="tickets" href="#">
                  Get your tickets
                  <svg class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg>
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="feature__media">
            <img src="../../assets/img/forum/Funding-the-Commons-Forum-SF-2026-6.jpg" alt="Participants working together on a laptop at Funding the Commons San Francisco" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="section tracks tracks--titled" aria-labelledby="tracks-title">
  <div class="section__inner">
    <div class="grid">
      <h2 id="tracks-title" class="tracks__title t-h2">The program</h2>
      <div class="tracks__intro t-h5" data-reveal>
        <p>Transformative AI will change economies, governments, and daily life as much as the industrial revolution did, in a fraction of the time. <span class="ink-60">It will reach everything public goods touch, including who works and gets paid, who is cared for and taught, who owns the data and the models, and who answers for the decisions made with it.</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="tracks__list tracks__list--side">

        <h3 class="track__name track__name--01 t-h4">Human Welfare Track</h3>
        <article class="track track--01" aria-label="Human Welfare track">
          <p class="track__title t-h2">What needs building, and will it reach everyone?</p>
          <p class="track__lead">The public goods of the age, one domain at a time: care, knowledge, nature, culture, civic life, and survival itself. For each, the funder's questions: where does money do the most for human welfare and the living world it depends on, are there builders ready to use it, and how will we know it worked.</p>
          <div class="track__tags">
            <span class="tag t-tag">Public AI and digital<br>public infrastructure</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Biosecurity and<br>pandemic preparedness</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Care, health,<br>and education</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Knowledge, data,<br>and science</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Planetary health and<br>resilient systems</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Culture, media,<br>and the arts</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Data rights and<br>compensation</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Work, income, and<br>the share of the gains</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Participation, community,<br>and civic life</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <h3 class="track__name track__name--02 t-h4">Human Agency Track</h3>
        <article class="track track--02" aria-label="Human Agency track">
          <p class="track__title t-h2">Who owns it, who decides, and who does it answer to?</p>
          <p class="track__lead">Power, through sovereignty, governance, and agency: who can switch the infrastructure off, who decides and answers for it, and whether people are still free to act. For funders, the same questions: where is this work underfunded, who can carry it, and how do we measure what the money did.</p>
          <div class="track__tags">
            <span class="tag t-tag">Sovereign AI,<br>data, and compute</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Open models</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Education and<br>knowledge infrastructure</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Governance of<br>frontier systems</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Concentration<br>of power</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">AI safety and<br>loss of control</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Verifiable AI and<br>accountability</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Information integrity<br>and provenance</span>
            <span class="tag t-tag">Digital human rights,<br>privacy, and identity</span>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="section formats formats--titled" aria-labelledby="formats-title" data-show="forumFormats">
  <div class="band" data-band="forumInstitutions" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="section__inner">
    <div class="grid">
      <h2 id="formats-title" class="formats__title t-h2">What to expect<br>as a participant or a speaker</h2>
      <div class="formats__lead t-h5" data-reveal><p>Expect to take part. <span class="ink-60">Your argument gets tested, your solution gets used, and the conversations are candid enough to change your mind. Every session is curated across fields, so a workshop on data rights might bring together an economist, a city official, and a researcher from an AI lab. Workshops put your work in the hands of the people who would use it. Debates run on the record or off. Funding rounds move real money, and the participants decide where it goes. Some sessions run under the Chatham House Rule, so people can argue freely at a time when public discourse rarely allows it.</span></p></div>
      <div class="formats__cards">

        <article class="format">
          <p class="t-meta">01</p>
          <div class="format__head">
            <h3 class="t-h4">Keynotes</h3>
            <p class="t-body-mono">Short talks from the people building the models, mechanisms, and policies.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="format">
          <p class="t-meta">02</p>
          <div class="format__head">
            <h3 class="t-h4">Debates and panels</h3>
            <p class="t-body-mono">Positions argued openly. Some sessions on the record, some off it.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="format">
          <p class="t-meta">03</p>
          <div class="format__head">
            <h3 class="t-h4">Hands-on workshops</h3>
            <p class="t-body-mono">Bring a model, a mechanism, or a vision and leave with it tested by the people who would use it.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="format">
          <p class="t-meta">04</p>
          <div class="format__head">
            <h3 class="t-h4">Live experiments</h3>
            <p class="t-body-mono">Funding rounds, votes, and prototypes run together with participants.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


